  <div class="article-layout">
    <div class="article-body" itemprop="articleBody">
      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>{{ t.verified }} species verified</strong> at one water bowl in a private backyard in Kota city
          between the evening of {{ d.period.from }} and {{ d.period.to }}:
          {{ t.byGroup.Bird }} birds, {{ t.byGroup.Mammal }} mammals and {{ t.byGroup.Amphibian }} amphibian.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>{{ t.onCamera }} were seen on camera and {{ t.heardOnly }} are known only by sound</strong>, from
          {{ t.cameraVisits }} camera visits and {{ t.soundRecords }} sound records.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A shy winter visitor kept coming back:</strong> a Bluethroat on {{ d.notable.bluethroat.cameraDays }}
          of {{ d.notable.bluethroat.daysSinceFirst }} days, mostly late in the afternoon.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Surprises:</strong> a White-breasted Waterhen, a Rhesus Macaque and a Sulphur-bellied Warbler.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>How far it goes:</strong> one spot, one season, and names that I checked alone. The counts are
          visits and calls, not animals.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The place and the days</h2>
      <p>
        The bowl is about half a metre across and stands on the ground in a private backyard in Kota city,
        Rajasthan. A fig tree stands in the same yard. The yard is not inside Mukundara Hills Tiger Reserve.
      </p>
      <p>
        Recording began on the evening of {{ d.period.from }} 2026, and this report uses the records up to
        {{ d.asOf.time }} on {{ d.asOf.date }}: {{ d.period.daysWord }} calendar days of early winter. The air at the
        node was between {{ d.weatherRange.min }} and {{ d.weatherRange.max }}&nbsp;°C, and the rain plate was wet on
        {{ d.weatherRange.wetDaysWord }} days.
      </p>

      <h2>How the records were made</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>The device.</strong> <a href="/falcon/">FALCON</a> Build 1: a 1080p USB camera with infrared
          lights about a metre from the bowl, a microphone board inside the box, a sensor for temperature, humidity
          and air pressure, and a rain plate. One cable runs to a computer indoors.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The models.</strong> MegaDetector V6 finds animals in the picture. BioCLIP 2.5 suggests a species
          from the 1,384 recorded in Rajasthan on iNaturalist. BirdNET V2.4 names bird calls. They suggest a name.
          They do not decide.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The units.</strong> A camera visit is one stay of an animal in the picture. A sound record is one
          stretch of calling by one species. Neither counts individual animals.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Checking.</strong> I watched or listened to every record counted here. A species counts only
          where I confirmed the suggested name or corrected it, under the name I gave. Everything else is left out.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Effort.</strong> The node sent sensor readings in all {{ d.effort.readingsHours }} hours. The
          software that analyses picture and sound was running for about {{ d.effort.shareLow }} to
          {{ d.effort.shareHigh }}&nbsp;% of that time ({{ d.effort.analysingLow }} to {{ d.effort.analysingHigh }}
          hours). Six known gaps of about two to five hours fell on {{ d.effort.gapDays }}, all by day or in the
          evening, and visits in those hours were missed. For two stretches that began at night
          ({% for u in d.effort.uncertain %}{{ u.fromDate }}, {{ u.from }} to {% if not u.sameDay %}{{ u.toDate }}, {% endif %}{{ u.to }}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %})
          the records do not show whether it was running.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Left out on purpose.</strong> People and vehicles in the picture are not counted. Insects at
          night cannot be named with this camera. Rats at night are no longer logged, for the reason given under
          limits.
        </li>
      </ul>

