      <h3>The Bluethroat</h3>
      <p>
        The Bluethroat (<em>{{ d.notable.bluethroat.sci }}</em>) is a winter visitor here, and a shy one. FALCON
        first recorded it at {{ d.notable.bluethroat.time }} on {{ d.notable.bluethroat.date }}. From then to
        24&nbsp;November it came on {{ d.notable.bluethroat.cameraDays }} of the
        {{ d.notable.bluethroat.daysSinceFirst }} days: {{ d.notable.bluethroat.visits }} visits, with
        {{ words[d.notable.bluethroat.longestRun] }} days in a row from 20 to 23&nbsp;November. It came mostly late, {{ d.notable.bluethroat.afternoon }} of the
        {{ d.notable.bluethroat.visits }} visits between 15:00 and 17:00. The microphone never picked it up. FALCON
        counts visits, not birds, so the {{ d.notable.bluethroat.visits }} visits may all be one individual.
      </p>

      <h3>Surprise visitors</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>White-breasted Waterhen</strong> (<em>{{ d.notable.waterhen.sci }}</em>),
          {{ d.notable.waterhen.date }}, {{ d.notable.waterhen.time }}: one visit by a bird of wet ground.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Rhesus Macaque</strong> (<em>{{ d.notable.macaque.sci }}</em>), {{ d.notable.macaque.date }},
          {{ d.notable.macaque.time }}: the first monkey on FALCON's record. The footage shows at least one animal.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Sulphur-bellied Warbler</strong> (<em>{{ d.notable.warbler.sci }}</em>),
          {{ d.notable.warbler.date }}, two visits from {{ d.notable.warbler.time }}. I saw and photographed one
          last year too.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Common Skittering Frog</strong> (<em>Euphlyctis cyanophlyctis</em>), 9&nbsp;November, 18:11: the
          only amphibian.
        </li>
      </ul>
