      <h3>Heard, not seen</h3>
      <p>
        {{ words[t.heardOnly] | capitalize }} species never came into the camera's view and are known only from their calls.
        Rose-ringed Parakeets, drawn by the fig tree, account for
        {% for row in d.table %}{% if row.name == "Rose-ringed Parakeet" %}{{ row.sound }} of the {{ t.soundRecords }} sound records and were heard on {{ row.days }} of the {{ d.period.days }} days{% endif %}{% endfor %}.
        The list also holds birds of open water, such as Black-winged Stilt and Eurasian Coot, that were heard
        calling and never seen. {{ words[t.heardSingle] | capitalize }} species rest on a single recording each: Asian Koel, Eurasian
        Moorhen, Grey Wagtail and Large Cuckooshrike. That is the thinnest evidence in this list.
      </p>

      <h3>Time of day</h3>
