      <h2>Limits</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>The names are mine alone.</strong> Nobody else has checked them. Two of the records are on
          iNaturalist, where other people can check the name: an
          <a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/415043198" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Oriental Magpie-Robin</a>
          and a
          <a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/415042739" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bluethroat</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>From the picture, the names are the weak point.</strong> With this webcam the suggested name was
          often wrong, and I named most camera visits myself from the recordings. The picture is poor in low light,
          pink on many mornings because the camera's infrared filter switches late, and it was red on
          23&nbsp;November after the camera's settings were reset. A Bluethroat's throat did not look blue. I put
          this down to the camera, not to the models.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>By sound, the names hold, with one caution.</strong> BirdNET's name was right for {{ d.sound.right }}
          of the {{ d.sound.real }} verified sound records ({{ d.sound.percent }}&nbsp;%). That figure covers real
          bird calls only. Street and household noise is still sometimes named as a bird, and I discarded those
          records on review.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No share of false records.</strong> Discarded records are deleted soon after review, so I cannot
          say what share of all records was false, for picture or for sound.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Rats spoiled five nights.</strong> I put grain near the bowl. Hardly any bird used it, only House
          Sparrows and Laughing Doves, and from 19&nbsp;November rats raided it every night: at least
          {% for n in d.rats %}{% if loop.last %}and {% endif %}{{ n.visits }}{% if loop.revindex0 > 1 %}, {% elif not loop.last %} {% endif %}{% endfor %} visits on the {{ words[d.rats.length] }} nights to
          23&nbsp;November.
          Their records were deleted, rats at night are no longer logged, and there will be no more feed near
          the bowl.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A correction.</strong> An earlier version of the project page listed a Rusty-spotted Cat. That was
          the model's name for the neighbourhood's domestic cat, and it is withdrawn.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>What this is not.</strong> It is not a census. One bowl, {{ d.period.daysWord }} days and one season
          say nothing about numbers of animals, and a species missing from the table may simply not have come to
          this spot.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What the device has achieved</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>{{ d.period.daysWord | capitalize }} days of recording at one spot, by day and by night, with the sensors reporting in every hour.</li>
        <li>Every record keeps its own evidence: a recording of the visit or the call, and the weather at that moment.</li>
        <li>Sound more than doubled the list: {{ t.heardOnly }} of the {{ t.verified }} species were never seen on camera.</li>
        <li>It recorded what is easy to miss: the hours a shy Bluethroat keeps, and a waterhen and a macaque at the bowl.</li>
        <li>It runs on parts anyone can buy and on freely available models, and <a href="{{ falconProject.repoUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the code is open source</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What changes next</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Camera.</strong> An 8-megapixel weatherproof network camera with its own infrared takes the place
          of the webcam. It is meant to deal with the low light, the wrong colours and the pink mornings.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Microphone.</strong> A new microphone takes over from the one on the board inside the box. It is
          meant to hear bird calls more clearly.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Paid for by supporters.</strong> Both were bought with the support FALCON has received, and both
          will share the single cable.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Not proven yet.</strong> They are tried on the desk first. Results with the new parts will follow
          on the <a href="/falcon/">FALCON page</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Later.</strong> A small computer in place of the desktop PC, and printed parts in place of the
          hand-made ones. <a href="/falcon/#support">Both still need support</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

